# Inventory roles & page guides

## Read first

- `_System_Core/problems/fixes/packaging-inventory-roles.md`
- `_System_Core/problems/fixes/inventory-role-permissions.md`
- `_System_Core/problems/fixes/page-guide-button-modal.md`
- `_System_Core/005_SPA_UX_Patterns.md` — §Page guide button, §Role-based inventory permissions, §Packaging and materials inventory pages

## Supplies roles (canonical)

| Role | Actions |
|------|---------|
| **HR** | Add item, stock in lot, **issue request** (approval required) |
| **Production manager** | View only |
| **Executive** | All HR actions + set on-hand; approve/deny on Requests |

`supply_detail.permissions` from API. Guides: `SuppliesInventoryGuideModal`, `InventoryRequestsGuideModal`.

## Packaging Materials roles (canonical)

| Role | Actions |
|------|---------|
| **HR** | Stock in lot only |
| **Production manager** | Deduct for use only |
| **Executive** | All + set on-hand + pool yield + catalog + extended activity log |

Enforce in `material_inventory.php` helpers + `materials.php` API. Return `permissions` from `packaging_detail`. Do not reintroduce HR count-fix requests on the packaging page.

## Product Costing

**Executive only** — `routes.ts`, `Sidebar.tsx`, `costing.php` (`api_require_role(['executive'])`). Never link HR or prod manager to `/costing` in guides or copy.

## Page guides (mandatory pattern)

- **Guide** button in `PageLayout` `actions` (muted border, `BookOpen` icon) — same classes as `CostingPage.tsx`
- Opens `*GuideModal` (`AppModal`, default **closed**)
- Role-specific content inside modal via `useAuth().role`
- **Never** inline collapsible guide panels on the page body

## New inventory features

1. PHP role helper → API gate → `permissions` in detail response
2. SPA buttons driven by permissions
3. Update the page `*GuideModal` (`PackagingInventoryGuideModal`, `SuppliesInventoryGuideModal`, `InventoryRequestsGuideModal`, `ParagisProductionGuideModal`, `DeptRawProduceGuideModal`) for affected roles
4. **Dept raw materials** (`RawDeptMaterialPage`): Paragis raw/WIP records are separate from finished barcode stock-in. Scanning pouches credits finished inventory only and does not require or deduct raw bags, WIP, or packaging. BRC/Jar retain their existing barcode stock-in behavior. Guides: [[fixes/dept-raw-guidance-and-mobile-honey]] · [[records/2026-09-09_raw-materials-ui-fix]]
5. Append `_System_Core/002_Memory_Bank.md` + fix note under `problems/fixes/` if pattern is reusable
